WEBVTT

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:10.000
<v Nadia Roy>Thanks for making time, Marc. I want to understand how online renewal changes the work for your processing officers.</v>

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:17.000
<v Marc Tremblay>Sure. Today my officers pull the paper file for every renewal and check it against the scanned copy.</v>

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:26.000
<v Marc Tremblay>With the new system they will review renewal applications on screen in the case management system, so nobody touches paper any more.</v>

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.000
<v Nadia Roy>How confident are they with the case management system today?</v>

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:38.000
<v Marc Tremblay>Most of them have only used it to look things up. Working a whole file in it is new for about forty officers.</v>

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:47.000
<v Marc Tremblay>Eligibility checks used to be manual. The system will flag eligibility automatically and officers only handle the exceptions.</v>

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:51.000
<v Nadia Roy>Does that change anything for your senior officers?</v>

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:59.000
<v Marc Tremblay>Yes. My senior officers will need to approve eligibility overrides in the system, which is a new step for them.</v>

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:07.000
<v Marc Tremblay>Decision letters will be generated from templates instead of being typed in Word, so that part gets easier.</v>

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.000
<v Nadia Roy>What worries you most about the change?</v>

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:20.000
<v Marc Tremblay>Honestly the biggest worry is the first month, when we run paper and online side by side and people switch between both.</v>

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:24.000
<v Nadia Roy>That is really helpful. Thank you, Marc.</v>
